# DuckLog Data Model and Persistence

## Core Models

### JournalEntry
```swift
@Model
class JournalEntry: Identifiable {
    var id: UUID
    var timestamp: Date
    var title: String
    var content: String
    var tags: [String]
    var status: String
    var isTrashed: Bool = false
    // Relationships
    var linkedPR: GitHubPR?
}
```

### GitHubPR
```swift
@Model
class GitHubPR: Identifiable {
    var id: String
    var title: String
    var description: String
    var status: String
    var url: URL
}
```

### JiraTicket
```swift
struct JiraTicket {
    var key: String
    var title: String
    var description: String
    var status: String
    var statusType: JiraStatusType
    var url: URL
}

enum JiraStatusType {
    case inProgress
    case done
    case blocked
    case other
    
    var color: Color { ... }
    var entryStatus: String { ... }
}
```

### SettingsModel
```swift
struct SettingsModel {
    var templateSections: [String]
    var sectionOrder: [String]
    var summaryTemplateEnabled: Bool
    
    // Jira settings
    var jiraInstanceURL: String
    var jiraUsername: String
    var jiraAPIToken: String
    var useMockJiraData: Bool
}
```

## Persistence Strategy

1. **SwiftData**
   - Used for all core models (JournalEntry, GitHubPR)
   - Handles relationships automatically
   - Supports standard CRUD operations

2. **UserDefaults**
   - Used for app settings and preferences
   - Stores non-sensitive configuration

3. **Keychain** (for sensitive data)
   - Stores API tokens and credentials securely
   - Used for Jira authentication

## Query Patterns

1. **Journal Entries**
   - Filter by date range: `entries.filter(#Predicate { $0.timestamp >= startDate && $0.timestamp <= endDate })`
   - Filter by tags: `entries.filter(#Predicate { $0.tags.contains(tag) })`
   - Filter by status: `entries.filter(#Predicate { $0.status == status })`
   - Filter by trash status: `entries.filter(#Predicate { $0.isTrashed == false })`
   - Sort by date: `entries.sort(by: { $0.timestamp > $1.timestamp })`

2. **Data Relationships**
   - One-to-one between JournalEntry and GitHubPR
   - Many-to-many between JournalEntry and tags (represented as string array)

## Best Practices

1. **Model Updates**
   - Use modelContext.insert() for new entries
   - Changes to properties are automatically tracked
   - Call modelContext.save() after batches of changes
   - Handle errors appropriately

2. **SwiftData Migration**
   - Plan for schema evolution
   - Use versioned schema when model changes
   - Test migration paths

3. **Mock Data**
   - Provide mock implementations for testing
   - Support offline mode where applicable 